"""OUI -> cleaned vendor name, for client fingerprinting's low-confidence tier
(wlan/fingerprint.py): every registered vendor, since naming who made a device --
without claiming which kind -- is the entire point of that tier.

Keys vary in length: most are 6 hex chars (a plain 24-bit OUI), some are 7 or 9 (IEEE's
finer-grained 28-/36-bit sub-allocations, where a single 24-bit block is actually split
between several organizations). fingerprint.py tries the longest prefix first.

GENERATED by scripts/generators/gen_fingerprint_vendors.py from Wireshark's weekly
manuf feed (wireshark.org/download/automated/data/manuf, GPLv2). Do NOT edit by hand;
rerun the script to refresh.
"""

